  "instruction_layer": {
    "inline": [
      "Use this parent only after a complete guide-issued mf_batch_parallel action_input binds the coordination row and at least two exact child backlog rows.",
      "Run side-effect-free Batch preflight before fan-out; do not write a durable queue when preflight returns blockers.",
      "Create one row-scoped mf_parallel successor per child; workers never implement against the Batch parent.",
      "Open or resume the durable integration epoch only at the exact target ref and base; merge only the server-selected queue prefix.",
      "After every integration generation run one current-HEAD full reconcile, then fresh authenticated postmerge QA for each child.",
      "If postmerge QA is NO-PASS, preserve the terminal source queue row and immutable first-generation history; allocate at most one fresh failed_qa_rework RuntimeContext in the same child Contract, perform one repair merge, then a new reconcile and fresh QA. Otherwise stop with terminal refusal.",
      "Never treat bypass or waive as candidate custody, landing, deployment, QA PASS or close authority.",
      "Close children through their own protected Gates; close the coordination row and release the epoch only when every child is FIXED and the parent close Gate accepts the exact Batch result."
    ],
